WEBVTT

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.300
I am myself alone.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.720
Therefore, demon,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.480
refashion my mind to suit my body!

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.440
I that have neither pity, love, nor fear

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.900
shall send all who wish our house's
downfall straight to the pits of hell!

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.360
Behold our sun!

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.740
The winter of our discontent has passed!

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.250
Well? What do you think?

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.330
You look lovely, Princess Elizabeth.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.750
Ugh! Elizabeth is my mother's name.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.670
Call me "Beth."

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.800
You're making quite the effort.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.300
Do you fancy some gentleman in attendance?

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.840
It's n-nothing like--

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.470
Are you hurt, my lady?

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.980
Uncle Richard!

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.900
Beth. You've grown into a
fine lady since I last saw you.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.360
Anne! Tell Richard to visit
London more often!

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.410
Come this way.
The banquet is about to start.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.160
Another day of ridiculous farce.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.720
York of the white rose.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.300
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:45.770
These royal houses with roses
for their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.480
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.210
Welcome, one and all!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.330
Let us enjoy our summer!

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.000
God save King Edward IV!

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.920
God save King Edward IV!

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.590
Look, Father! A dragon!

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.300
Kill it! Kill it, Saint George!

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.770
Kill it! Kill it! Kill it!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.180
But the script says--

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.270
Stand aside!

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.940
George! George!

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.020
Hooray!

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.940
Your Royal Highnesses,

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:04.610
your servant George, Duke of Clarence,
has slain the wicked dragon!

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.580
George! Are you drunk?!
Sheathe your sword!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.460
You seem quite displeased
that I've reduced your authority.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.710
Shut up.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.010
Richard. Have you been well?

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:31.270
I have. How is your wife?

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.310
Mine is concerned for her as well.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.770
She's well, thanks to you.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.190
God took pity on me for losing
lands to my little brother

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.070
and blessed us with children.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:46.450
Speaking of which, you're taking
a long time to make a second!

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.080
Don't tell me you're neglecting Anne.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:53.000
Rumor has it that you've never
shared a bed since you married her.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.040
Whose child is your only son?
Let's check if he looks like--

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.380
I don't feel well.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.340
Please excuse me.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.170
Here is what you've all been waiting for!
The "cakes of destiny"!

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.890
Please reach under the cloth
and take a cake!

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:10.140
The shape of your cake
predicts your future!

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.640
Fortune telling? Hogwash.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.560
Hey! Bring me more wine!

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.730
For once, I agree with George.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.200
How does this shape appear to you?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.660
Hm...

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.870
What is it?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.200
I've got it! It's a horseshoe!

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.870
Oh! I know, Father!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.750
It's a letter G!

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.250
I beg your pardon!

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:46.760
It was the children's fault,
and more importantly...

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:50.640
Hastings, provide that good
woman with a new dress.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.060
Of course.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.140
Come with me.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.650
The Duke of Gloucester,

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.450
Richard Plantagenet.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.280
A bloodstained G, is it?

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.200
Buckingham. That isn't my future.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.700
Then choose one for yourself.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.750
I merely obey my sovereign.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:22.340
With whose policy you seemed dissatisfied
in the recent French campaign.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.670
Mind your tongue.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:29.930
If you're thinking of Warwick's murder,
some lay the blame at Richard's feet.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:34.890
I've long admired your virtue, Richard.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:39.060
I'll make the choice with you.
We'll pick out your future.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.030
Take any dress you like.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.400
His Majesty bid me say as much.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.200
I'll wait outside the door.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.870
But I can hardly change
dresses all on my own.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:01.080
Would you lend me a hand?

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.550
What say I assist you?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.680
Your Majesty!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:17.470
At first glance,
I knew what lurks within you.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.390
Beauty and debauchery.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:22.190
Your Majesty, I have a husband.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.020
All the better.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.980
Join us, Hastings.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.190
Wait!

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:30.110
Please wait, Your Majesty!

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.490
Have you ever made use of this?

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:37.330
It is a miraculous elixir that inspires
sweet, licentious passion.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.920
Who are you?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.210
My name is Jane.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:49.550
Have you ever slept with a witch,
Your Royal Majesty?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.470
Can a witch predict the future?

00:07:55.470 --> 00:08:00.140
She can read signs. Such as...

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:04.020
...those "cakes of destiny," for example.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.780
He spent last night alone as well.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:17.620
This body makes even
wishing for a wife a sin.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.160
Or so I thought.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.120
Shouldn't I join you?

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.670
You would only end up
feeling unwell again.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:28.800
Father.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.970
Richard, hold him before you set out.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.600
You look as lovely as always.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:44.770
Flowers should go to your mother,

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.020
Edward.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.030
Farewell.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.610
Let's see your father off.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:01.450
He truly looks more like <i>him </i>every year.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:06.170
I feel as though Richard reproaches me
every time he says Edward's name.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:10.090
As though our loveless days
are the price I must pay.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:13.050
You left your wife behind?

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.630
As did you.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.510
I sleep with her enough from day to day.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:20.930
The soul and the body
are separate matters.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.270
I suppose.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:28.270
If God gave us flesh to punish us,

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.810
then after all,

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:33.740
this body is just a prison of the soul...

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:37.610
The death of my soul brought me peace.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:41.950
I would never have been
imprisoned without it.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.750
Nothing beats drinking wine with my son.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.880
Look! I drained it in no time!

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.090
George, why don't you drink a little less?

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.460
I hear you used wild words at the banquet.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.260
I only spoke the truth!

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.130
Let me prophecy, my unfortunate son!

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:02.510
By the time you inherit, our house will be
reduced to penniless country gentlemen!

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.060
That's quite enough!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.440
I'm sorry.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.480
Everything I do turns out wrong.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.530
There's no hope left for me.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:19.950
George, you aren't hopeless at all.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:23.200
You ought by all rights to rival the king.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.410
Isabelle.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:30.960
No matter how much you hate him,
you mustn't let it show.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.920
Don't worry, and have faith in me.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:39.720
I chose to stand by you,
even after you turned on my father.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.300
I even sacrificed my own sister.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.890
I've prepared what Your Grace requested.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.690
Will it really work?

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.440
It will, Your Grace.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.530
However,

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.900
every curse comes at a price.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.450
I don't care.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:04.830
It doesn't matter if I get to be queen.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.790
You mean everything to me,

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.750
my George.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.180
How's that?!

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.930
Marvelous, Your Highness!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:26.390
How idiotic. He really is
a child if he enjoys that.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.100
George never came.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:34.650
I doubt he was invited. Hardly surprising
after the way he behaved last time.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:36.570
And not only last time.

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:40.110
Father! Look at this!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.110
I see.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:47.660
It's nearly nightfall.
You should be in bed.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:48.750
I'd still like to--

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:52.830
Take tonight to rest after
these days of feasting.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:55.840
Would you find my presence inconvenient?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.300
Did you say something?

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.050
Nothing at all.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.220
So, the queen's spell has broken at last.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.350
Another new witch
must have taken her place.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.310
Yes. This is nothing unusual.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:16.270
Still, while he's had
new favorites before,

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:19.480
he's never neglected me for any of them.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.700
It doesn't matter.
I no longer need the king's love.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.210
Mother?

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.710
I hold the winning hand:

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.300
my sons who will ascend the throne.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:43.840
Now, gentlemen,
the remainder of the night is ours!

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.350
That woman.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:53.310
Your Grace, please drink your fill.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:03.360
My lords, I have prepared this
miraculous wine specially for tonight!

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.240
Welcome to Elysium!

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:19.170
He calls this "Elysium"?

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.920
To your brother, I suppose it is.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:29.050
I believed that paradise
and light lay within that circlet.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.930
Within that circlet lies paradise.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.350
What?

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.940
My head is spinning.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:37.980
Richard.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.860
Father?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.280
Join us.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:49.370
Richard, this is paradise.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:53.500
Yes, Richard. Have your fill of pleasure.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.080
Relax your inhibitions.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.250
Stop.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.750
Please stop.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:06.130
Demon! Demon! Demon!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.510
My soul perished back then,

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:12.100
and yet it was so easily recalled.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.470
--What a feeble "death."
--Hey! Richard!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.770
Hang on!

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:20.400
They're mad.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.230
This is no paradise.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.490
That man...

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.900
That man...

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.910
...is not my father.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.250
Where am I?

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.290
I remember nothing more.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.590
Did someone touch this body of mine?

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.590
Your Grace.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:49.720
Catesby.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:55.180
Please forgive my impertinence.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:57.180
The guests have dispersed.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:00.190
I doubt anyone remembers
what happened last night.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.270
Thank you.

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:06.610
I wish that I could have warned you.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:10.160
Lord Hastings told me
that His Majesty's lover,

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:14.990
a woman called Jane,
can compound a variety of drugs.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.830
You're more attuned to
court gossip than I am now.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:23.420
My master, Lord Hastings,
is an intimate of the king.

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.510
I'm in your debt.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:29.880
Your Grace, about that day--

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.220
Don't speak of it! It's over!

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.310
It all came to an end that day.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.730
That aside, tell me about Jane.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:43.060
This is merely a rumor,

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:47.280
but she apparently
termed herself a "witch."

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.740
A witch.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:55.620
After tasting this, ordinary lovemaking
becomes merely a chore.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.410
What once seemed to shine so brightly

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.580
always loses its luster
once it becomes mine.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.500
Your Majesty.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.710
But Jane is different.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.300
The more I have of her, the more I want.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:12.340
She'll lead me from this
dull throne to Elysium.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:15.970
Is something the matter?

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.680
I've felt my health
declining rapidly of late.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.690
Especially the day after my enjoy--

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.310
Your Majesty!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.270
I'm merely a bit tired.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.270
Now, would you summon Jane for me?

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:31.700
I'm certain that she'll give me
unlimited strength.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:38.370
Fetch Jane. I'll keep watch
at His Majesty's side.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.660
I doubt it's serious,

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:45.630
but don't let the court, and especially
Queen Elizabeth, hear of this.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.800
I want to know who that woman really is.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.590
If she is a witch, I'll simply...

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:57.640
Your Grace.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:02.430
This is no festival.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.440
Picture it in your mind.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.440
And pray.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.270
Pray!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:08.060
Cast your anger and resentment...

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.980
...into this fire!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.410
What's this?

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.950
"Death to King Edward"?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.870
That's a cursed doll.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:32.010
I wonder who could have
wished death on His Majesty.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.010
F-Forgive me,

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.380
O Lord.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.720
Isabelle! Are you all right?!
This is so sudden!

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.350
Her health has never
recovered from childbirth.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:44.430
She gave birth more than six months ago!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.520
I suspect that stress is also to blame.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.770
Hang on, Isabelle!

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:54.150
Your Majesty, I can venture a guess
at the cause of your ailment.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.200
At the identity of the one who cursed you.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.950
My medicine... There...

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:06.540
Isabelle, all I've ever
done is let you down.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.630
I'm truly sorry.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.210
But I swear...

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:14.260
Let me swear that
I'll turn over a new leaf.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.390
Cursing the king would
be the gravest of crimes!

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.020
Who is it? Tell me their name.

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:30.770
Your Majesty, do you remember
the "cakes of destiny"?

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:35.740
Red wine stands for blood,
and the capital G is an initial.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.740
It can't be.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:41.530
But it is. Bloodstained George.

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:45.700
I love you, Isabelle.
We'll always be together.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.330
Right, Isabelle?

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.130
Isabelle? Isabelle!

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:57.090
But without proof...

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.880
Your Majesty, I have the proof here.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.510
What's this?!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.810
Those three dolls contained slips of paper

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:11.100
bearing wishes for the death
of Your Majesty and the princes.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.650
But this isn't George's writing.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.360
Your Majesty, entrust this matter to me.

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:20.200
I will question George about
the truth behind this "curse."

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:25.080
What are you after?

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:30.330
Is your plan to frame George
to convince me that you're a witch?

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.830
Who can say?

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:35.210
You won't escape suspicion.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:41.130
The witch who made the palace a den
of vice will burn like Joan of Arc.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:44.890
Did I make it a den of vice?

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:49.730
The king has forgotten war and
cares more for lust than his realm.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:51.850
His younger brother is a sot

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:56.360
whose emotional outbursts make him
the House of York's Achilles' heel.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.610
Am I wrong?

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.190
What's your point?

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:01.490
I've taken an interest in you.

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:06.410
Unlike other men, what's within
you promises complexity.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.040
Know your place!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:12.210
Merely a jest.
Nobles seek meaning in everything.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:16.840
I have no goals;
I simply wish to enjoy life.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:22.380
I'll go on alone from here.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:25.350
--But...
--If you swear allegiance to York,

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:28.260
forget this and depart!

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:32.520
If we let that witch live, she'll serve
as a check against the queen.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.820
George, however, is now only a thorn
in the House of York's side.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:40.650
And as he threatens York,

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.570
I will arrest George.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:51.710
Why didn't you invite me?

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:53.830
I've been looking for you.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:56.540
I saw you set out with your man.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.460
You overheard us?

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.800
However often you deny it--

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:03.130
Buckingham, assist me.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.510
You mean it?

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:08.850
Wait. There's something I must know first.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.810
Are you hiding anything from me?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.730
Swear that you have no secrets from me.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:19.190
If we're to be partners,
we must share everything.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.360
I swear it.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.200
In that case, Richard,

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:30.410
my king, order me, and I shall
grant your every wish.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:35.540
You're mistaken about one thing.
Catesby isn't my man.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:39.710
Is he not? He still seems
to be serving you admirably.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:46.300
As one who swears allegiance to York,
I will accompany you.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:48.600
As you wish.

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:49.680
Let's go.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:54.680
We'll eliminate those who would
harm York by any means necessary.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:58.310
I did touch it back then.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.980
I touched my future.
